# 88. My Strongest UX Recommendation

The biggest conceptual enhancement I would make to the current Lead Intelligence direction is to **stop thinking of the primary object as a “lead.”**

The UI should make three objects obvious:

### Prospect

> Someone/something we discovered.

### Intelligence

> What SmartSapp knows about it.

### Opportunity

> Why SmartSapp believes we should act.

That distinction gives the product a much stronger mental model:

```text
PROSPECT
ABC School
       ↓
INTELLIGENCE
Digital maturity 42
No payment system
Decision maker found
High similarity to customers
Recent signal
       ↓
OPPORTUNITY
Strong SmartSapp Pay opportunity
       ↓
ACTION
Contact proprietor
       ↓
CRM
Lead → Opportunity → Deal
       ↓
REVENUE
```

That is the UX architecture I would use to turn the current Lead Intelligence implementation into a **serious SmartSapp acquisition product rather than simply a more sophisticated lead finder**.

Most importantly, **the UI should be implemented in the same phase order as the backend architecture**. Do not build the final navigation and all screens first and leave the underlying state/job/evidence model until later. Each phase should introduce the UX surface that exposes the corresponding domain capability, while preserving the same prospect profile, event timeline, scoring and CRM interaction patterns throughout.
